text:
Ten agents are now working in the background:
- five engine builders;
- one fresh check of the six revised I04 pages;
- three writer groups (data pages, I01, I02);
- the K06 check, if it recovered from the rate limit.

I'll pick up each result as it lands: record check passes, sync configs, rebind and run new page tickets, then send the next pages to writers.

Ledger updated. Still waiting on:
- E4's knowledge tests;
- E5's boundary rebuild;
- the three writer groups;
- the K06 check.

Now running:
- the I01 check and an I13 writer;
- the data and I02 writers;
- E4's knowledge tests and E5's boundary rebuild;
- the K06 check.

The batch is 32 tickets in, all exiting 0. When it and the builder follow-ups finish, one more pass will:
1. rerun the page tickets of the tasks the follow-ups changed;
2. wire the new partition probe tickets;
3. bind, sync configs and check.

All six I01 pages passed. I'm recording the passes, but they reopen for the age-wording fix the check didn't catch. The check also surfaced four contract gaps, which I'm fixing in the skills and the register:
- one cite reads a retired need;
- the checker never catches a cite of a retired need;
- the page tool files cite items under the wrong heading;
- the Information rules contradict each other on cites.

Ledger updated. Waiting on:
- the second pass (wiring, rerunning tickets, binding);
- the two checks;
- the I13 writer.

Eight agents are running:
- five writers: I08, K02, K03, K04 and K06;
- the I14 writer;
- two checks: data plus I02, and I13.

I'm holding the I03 writer back to stay under the rate limit and will dispatch it as slots free up.

The re-check is running. Waiting on it and on:
- the I08 and I03 checks;
- the I05, I06 and I07 writers;
- the K02 fix.

The ledger is updated. Waiting on:
- the K02-plus-I03 check;
- the I07, I15, I16, I11, single-I and K01 writers;
- the I05 fix.

The review returned small fixes for both files, and all of them are sound. I'm applying them now. The main ones:
- dates are written as the day, not the exact time;
- a column the dictionary doesn't list gets no range;
- E7 drops the `grain_flag` column it borrowed from E8;
- E8's null test is loosened so it can find the fields it is meant to find.

Round 4 agreed I03's question file. It found one last bug in the script: a partition with no patient keys at all crashed on a division by zero instead of being refused. The fix is one character: `if 0 < n < floor` became `if n < floor`. The reviewer is confirming it now.

## 📋 Summary and Next

On the reviewer's AGREE:
1. mark I03 agreed and rerun its six partitions;
2. the writer adds each partition's patient total to its page;
3. a separate check agent checks all six.
